{"type": "mcq", "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"x squared plus x StartRoot t EndRoot plus y squared minus y minus 65 equals 0\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>65</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The given equation, where <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math> is a constant, defines a circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane. The radius of this circle is <math alttext=\"StartRoot 83 EndRoot\"><msqrt>\n\t<mn>83</mn>\n</msqrt>\n</math>. What is the value of <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math>?</p>", "keys": ["ac85fa37-e92f-4759-8f44-e87040b2c819"], "answerOptions": [{"id": "85a45bcc-69bc-4bbf-bf03-b5ac8897f837", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"73\"><mn>73</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "ac85fa37-e92f-4759-8f44-e87040b2c819", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"71\"><mn>71</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "7081640e-ad0c-445a-b19d-eaf4cfcf8993", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"37\"><mn>37</mn>\n</math></p>"}, {"id": "8d07cbc4-ea57-4a48-9c21-3a22061ed018", "content": "<p><math alttext=\"35\"><mn>35</mn>\n</math></p>"}], "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. It's given that the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x squared plus x StartRoot t EndRoot plus y squared minus y minus 65 equals 0\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>65</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math> is a constant, defines a circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane. The equation of a circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane can be written in the form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals r squared\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis h comma k right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is the center and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> is the radius of the circle. Adding <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"65\"><mn>65</mn></math> to both sides of the given equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x squared plus x StartRoot t EndRoot plus y squared minus y equals 65\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>65</mn></math>. By completing the square, this equation can be rewritten as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x squared plus x StartRoot t EndRoot plus left parenthesis StartFraction StartRoot t EndRoot Over 2 EndFraction right parenthesis squared right parenthesis plus left parenthesis y squared minus y plus left parenthesis negative one half right parenthesis squared right parenthesis equals 65 plus left parenthesis StartFraction StartRoot t EndRoot Over 2 EndFraction right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis negative one half right parenthesis squared\"><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>65</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. This equation can be rewritten as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x squared plus x StartRoot t EndRoot plus StartFraction t Over 4 EndFraction right parenthesis plus left parenthesis y squared minus y plus one fourth right parenthesis equals 65 plus StartFraction t Over 4 EndFraction plus one fourth\"><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>65</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>, or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x plus StartFraction StartRoot t EndRoot Over 2 EndFraction right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus one half right parenthesis squared equals StartFraction 261 Over 4 EndFraction plus StartFraction t Over 4 EndFraction\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mi>t</mi></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>261</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>. Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r squared equals StartFraction 261 Over 4 EndFraction plus StartFraction t Over 4 EndFraction\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>261</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>. It's given that the radius of this circle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartRoot 83 EndRoot\"><msqrt><mn>83</mn></msqrt></math>; therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r equals StartRoot 83 EndRoot\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>83</mn></msqrt></math>. Squaring both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r squared equals 83\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>83</mn></math>. Since&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r squared equals StartFraction 261 Over 4 EndFraction plus StartFraction t Over 4 EndFraction\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>261</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r squared equals 83\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>83</mn></math>, it follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 261 Over 4 EndFraction plus StartFraction t Over 4 EndFraction equals 83\"><mfrac><mn>261</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>83</mn></math>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math> yields&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"261 plus t equals 332\"><mn>261</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>332</mn></math>. Subtracting&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"261\"><mn>261</mn></math> from both sides of this equation&nbsp;yields&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t equals 71\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>71</mn></math>. Therefore, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"71\"><mn>71</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>", "externalid": "0727e22f-f583-4696-b931-a7ab10b22425", "correct_answer": ["B"]}